From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: fix three HFI Gen1 encoder packets

Three HFI Gen1 encoder packets differ from what the firmware expects
(compared with venus, which drives the same firmwares):

1. The uncompressed EMPTY_BUFFER packet copied buf->flags, which holds
   V4L2_BUF_FLAG_* bits, into the HFI flags field. V4L2_BUF_FLAG_MAPPED
   is HFI_BUFFERFLAG_EOS and every queued buffer is mapped, so every
   input frame reached the firmware marked as end of stream, and
   V4L2_BUF_FLAG_KEYFRAME landed on HFI_BUFFERFLAG_DATACORRUPT. End of
   stream is sent as a drain command, so send 0, as upstream did before
   0021.
2. HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME has no payload, but the
   packet carried an extra u32. On SM8350 the firmware fails the session
   with HFI_ERR_SESSION_CMDSIZE at the first forced key frame.
3. HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_SESSION_QP_RANGE_V2 used 0xFFFFFFFF as the
   layer id. 0xFF means all layers (venus, and upstream before 0021).

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c     |   25 +++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 708dcd1..db80992 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -302,7 +302,13 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_queue_input_buffer(struct iris_inst *inst, struct iris_
 		uncom_ip_pkt.time_stamp_hi = upper_32_bits(buf->timestamp);
 		uncom_ip_pkt.time_stamp_lo = lower_32_bits(buf->timestamp);
 		uncom_ip_pkt.view_id = 0;
-		uncom_ip_pkt.flags = buf->flags;
+		/*
+		 * buf->flags holds V4L2_BUF_FLAG_* bits, which are not HFI buffer
+		 * flags: V4L2_BUF_FLAG_MAPPED is HFI_BUFFERFLAG_EOS, and every
+		 * queued buffer is mapped. End of stream goes to the firmware as
+		 * a drain command, so an input frame carries no flags.
+		 */
+		uncom_ip_pkt.flags = 0;
 		uncom_ip_pkt.mark_target = 0;
 		uncom_ip_pkt.mark_data = 0;
 		uncom_ip_pkt.offset = buf->data_offset;
@@ -658,8 +664,9 @@ iris_hfi_gen1_packet_session_set_property(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *p
 		if (min_qp > 0xff || max_qp > 0xff)
 			return -ERANGE;
 
-		range->min_qp.layer_id = 0xFFFFFFFF;
-		range->max_qp.layer_id = 0xFFFFFFFF;
+		/* 0xFF is "all layers", as in venus; 0xFFFFFFFF is not a layer id */
+		range->min_qp.layer_id = 0xFF;
+		range->max_qp.layer_id = 0xFF;
 		range->min_qp.qp_packed = (min_qp & 0xFF) | ((min_qp & 0xFF) << 8) |
 			((min_qp & 0xFF) << 16);
 		range->max_qp.qp_packed = (max_qp & 0xFF) | ((max_qp & 0xFF) << 8) |
@@ -745,13 +752,13 @@ iris_hfi_gen1_packet_session_set_property(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *p
 		packet->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32);
 		break;
 	}
-	case HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME: {
-		u32 *in = pdata;
-
-		packet->data[1] = *in;
-		packet->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32);
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME:
+		/*
+		 * The property has no payload on HFI Gen1, as in venus. Four
+		 * extra bytes make the firmware fail the session with
+		 * HFI_ERR_SESSION_CMDSIZE.
+		 */
 		break;
-	}
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VDEC_OUTPUT_ORDER: {
 		u32 *in = pdata;
 
